      "side": 1,
      "message": "I suppose this is fine but will also catch any change to `DEPS`. The way to do this in general (and more correctly) would be to have `build_tint.py` run `ninja -C $build_dir -tdeps` and massage that into a `.d` file (take every line that starts with four spaces, sort and unique them, then put them all on one long line that starts with `target: `) and then specify that `.d` file as the [`depfile`](https://gn.googlesource.com/gn/+/main/docs/reference.md#var_depfile).",
      "revId": "b8fad68823d010d8cb516b65046a7f2c2fb0debe",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8fda4bc9_f5af2629",
        "filename": "third_party/dawn/BUILD.gn",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 26,
      "author": {
        "id": 5395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-08T21:07:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I updated build_tint.py to output a .d file. Rather than use ninja to generate this, I used globs to approximate it (I could only get ninja to output stuff for the entire Dawn build, which seemed like overkill).",
      "parentUuid": "5e38c213_8ae28170",
      "revId": "b8fad68823d010d8cb516b65046a7f2c2fb0debe",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7b671908_5ef5bdea",
        "filename": "third_party/dawn/BUILD.gn",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 26,
      "author": {
        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-09T19:02:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It turns out that `ninja -tdeps` on a target only works if there was a `depfile` for that target. This is generally the case for our compile actions, but for most other targets it isn\u0027t. So generally one would need to use `ninja -tdeps \u003ctarget\u003e` to get the dynamic dependencies of a target (add those, if any), then use `ninja -tinputs \u003ctarget\u003e` to get the list of inputs (add those) and the recurse on the inputs.\n\nWhen `ninja -tdeps` is used at the top level one gets effectively the result of evaluating this recursively, since the output is the concatenation of everything done in a build. Unfortunately, `ninja` doesn\u0027t seem to have a tool to just do this recursive lookup for any given target directly.\n\nI\u0027d like to get this right because this might end up being a model for how Skia should shell out to build other things as well.",
      "parentUuid": "8fda4bc9_f5af2629",
      "revId": "b8fad68823d010d8cb516b65046a7f2c2fb0debe",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fe5b3e87_169c6f31",
        "filename": "third_party/dawn/BUILD.gn",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 26,
      "author": {
        "id": 5395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-11T15:32:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done. I made recursive calls to ninja -tinputs to accomplish this.\n\nThe generated .d file isn\u0027t perfect. For example, it doesn\u0027t include the .h files, likely because the tint GN rules don\u0027t list those, so if there was a header only change, we wouldn\u0027t notice and possiblely have a stale build.",
